oke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"menu__ext-link\" href=\"https://teletype.in/@ironvane/IronvanePass\" hreflang=\"ru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Ironvane Pass</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"12\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"12\"><path d=\"M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3v5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg></a></div><div class=\"menu__ext menu__ext--tight\" data-menu-ext=\"\"><span class=\"mono menu__ext-label\">On Telegram</span><a class=\"menu__ext-link\" href=\"https://t.me/+-lN8N8R_91UzYjc0\" hreflang=\"ru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Team chat</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"12\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"12\"><path d=\"M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3v5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"menu__foot\">\n<div class=\"menu__contact\">\n<span class=\"mono\">Language</span>\n<div class=\"menu__langs\"><a aria-current=\"true\" class=\"menu__lang\" data-lang=\"en\" href=\"/en/insights/finding-winning-angles/\" hreflang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flag\" focusable=\"false\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 12\"><use href=\"#flag-gb\"></use></svg>EN</a>\n<a aria-current=\"false\" class=\"menu__lang\" data-lang=\"ru\" href=\"/ru/insights/finding-winning-angles/\" hreflang=\"ru\" lang=\"ru\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flag\" focusable=\"false\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 12\"><use href=\"#flag-ru\"></use></svg>RU</a>\n<a aria-current=\"false\" class=\"menu__lang\" data-lang=\"uk\" href=\"/uk/insights/finding-winning-angles/\" hreflang=\"uk\" lang=\"uk\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flag\" focusable=\"false\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 12\"><use href=\"#flag-ua\"></use></svg>UK</a>\n<a aria-current=\"false\" class=\"menu__lang\" data-lang=\"es\" href=\"/es/insights/finding-winning-angles/\" hreflang=\"es\" lang=\"es\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flag\" focusable=\"false\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 12\"><use href=\"#flag-es\"></use></svg>ES</a>\n<a aria-current=\"false\" class=\"menu__lang\" data-lang=\"cs\" href=\"/cs/insights/finding-winning-angles/\" hreflang=\"cs\" lang=\"cs\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flag\" focusable=\"false\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 12\"><use href=\"#flag-cz\"></use></svg>CS</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"menu__contact\">\n<span class=\"mono\">General</span>\n<a href=\"mailto:hello@ironvane-media.com\">hello@ironvane-media.com</a>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div><div aria-labelledby=\"read-bar-label\" class=\"read-bar\" data-read-bar=\"\" hidden=\"\"><i></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\" id=\"read-bar-label\">Reading progress</span></div>", "main": "\n<article>\n<section class=\"article-hero\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"breadcrumb\" style=\"margin-bottom:26px\">\n<a href=\"/en/insights/\">Insights</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>Creative strategy</span>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"article-hero__meta\">\n<span class=\"article-hero__cat\">Creative strategy</span>\n<time class=\"num\" datetime=\"2026-07-14\">Jul 14, 2026</time>\n<span>8 min read</span>\n</div>\n<h1 class=\"article-hero__title balance\">Finding winning angles before you spend</h1>\n<p class=\"article-hero__lead pretty\">The best-performing ad in an account is rarely the most beautiful one. It is usually the one that names a belief the audience already held and had never seen written down.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"article-layout\">\n<aside class=\"article-toc\">\n<span class=\"article-toc__key\" id=\"article-toc-key\">In this article</span>\n<nav aria-labelledby=\"article-toc-key\" class=\"article-toc__list\"><a href=\"#s1\">An angle is a claim, not a format</a>\n<a href=\"#s2\">Where angles actually come from</a>\n<a href=\"#s3\">Scoring before testing</a>\n<a href=\"#s4\">One variable, one answer</a>\n<a href=\"#s5\">Angles expire; the map does not</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<div>\n<div class=\"prose\">\n<h2 id=\"s1\">An angle is a claim, not a format</h2>\n<p>Teams routinely confuse the two. A talking-head UGC video is a format. \"You will get approved before your coffee gets cold\" is an angle. Formats affect delivery cost; angles affect whether anyone cares. When a test result is filed under the format, the learning is lost — you know that UGC beat static, but not why, so nothing transfers to the next batch.</p>\n<p>Write angles as full sentences that could be argued with. If a stranger cannot disagree with your angle, it is not an angle — it is a category description.</p>\n<h2 id=\"s2\">Where angles actually come from</h2>\n<p>Not from a brainstorm. Four sources produce almost everything worth testing, and all four are available before you spend a euro.</p>\n<ol><li>Your own support tickets and sales calls. The objection that comes up most often in month one of ownership is the objection your ads should be answering.</li>\n<li>Cancellation and refund reasons. People are unusually honest when leaving. Each reason is an angle inverted — solve it in the ad and you pre-filter the cohort.</li>\n<li>Competitor reviews, especially three-star ones. Five-star reviews are marketing. One-star reviews are anger. Three-star reviews contain the trade-off the market is actually making.</li>\n<li>Search and store queries. The words people use when nobody is watching are the words your hook should use.</li></ol>\n<p class=\"callout balance\">A week of review mining routinely produces twenty angles. Three of them will carry the account for a year.</p>\n<h2 id=\"s3\">Scoring before testing</h2>\n<p>Twenty angles is too many to test properly at once — you would split the budget until nothing reaches significance. Score them on three axes and test the top handful first.</p>\n<ul><li>Reach — how many people in the market plausibly hold this belief? A true angle for two percent of the market cannot carry scale.</li>\n<li>Differentiation — can a competitor say the same sentence honestly? If yes, you are funding the category, not the brand.</li>\n<li>Provability — can the claim be demonstrated inside the first five seconds? Angles that require trust you have not earned yet convert badly cold.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"s4\">One variable, one answer</h2>\n<p>When the shortlist goes into production, keep everything except the claim as constant as the format allows. Same length, same pacing, same call to action, same landing page. This feels wasteful — you could be testing five things at once — but a test that changes three variables produces a winner you cannot explain, and an unexplainable winner cannot be extended.</p>\n<p>The point of angle testing is not to find one ad. It is to find the argument that works, so that the next twelve ads can be built from it with confidence.</p>\n<h2 id=\"s5\">Angles expire; the map does not</h2>\n<p>Markets move. An angle built on a price advantage dies the week a competitor matches it. Keep the angle map as a living document with a status against each entry — untested, validated, scaled, exhausted, blocked by compliance. After two quarters, that document is more valuable than the ad account itself, because it holds every conclusion you paid for.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"article-takeaways\" data-reveal=\"\">\n<p class=\"article-takeaways__key\">Takeaways</p>\n<ul class=\"tick-list\"><li>Write angles as arguable sentences, not format descriptions.</li>\n<li>Mine support tickets, churn reasons and three-star competitor reviews before brainstorming.</li>\n<li>Score for reach, differentiation and provability, then test the claim with everything else held constant.</li></ul>\n</div>\n<aside class=\"svc-links\" data-reveal=\"\">\n<p class=\"svc-links__key\">Related services</p>\n<a class=\"svc-link\" href=\"/en/services/#creative-strategy\">\n<span class=\"svc-link__num\">01</span>\n<span class=\"svc-link__body\"><span class=\"svc-link__title\">Creative Strategy</span><span class=\"svc-link__sum\">The messaging system that decides what every ad says, why it says it, and how long it stays alive.</span></span>\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"14\"><path d=\"M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3v5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg>\n</a>\n<a class=\"svc-link\" href=\"/en/services/#creative-production\">\n<span class=\"svc-link__num\">06</span>\n<span class=\"svc-link__body\"><span class=\"svc-link__title\">Creative Production</span><span class=\"svc-link__sum\">Production built for testing velocity, not for a showreel.</span></span>\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"14\"><path d=\"M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3v5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg>\n</a>\n</aside>\n<div class=\"article-foot\">\n<span class=\"article-foot__author\">Written by the Ironvane Media team</span>\n<button class=\"btn btn--ghost btn--sm\" data-copy=\"\" data-copy-done=\"Link copied\" data-copy-label=\"Copy link\" type=\"button\">Copy link</button>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</article>\n<section class=\"section section--line\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"section-head\" data-reveal=\"\">\n<div class=\"section-head__row\"><h2 class=\"h2 balance\">Related reading</h2><a class=\"link\" href=\"/en/insights/\"><span>All insights</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"12\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"12\"><path d=\"M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3v5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"></path></svg></a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"articles articles--3\" style=\"margin-top:36px\"><a class=\"card article-card\" data-article=\"\" data-category=\"creativeCat\" data-reveal=\"\" data-search=\"Why good creatives stop working Creative fatigue is usually diagnosed too late and treated with the wrong medicine. Here is what actually decays, how to see it three days earlier, and what to replace. Creative strategy\" href=\"/en/insights/why-good-creatives-stop-working/\">\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"article-card__cover\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"mark\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" preserveaspectratio=\"xMidYMid slice\" viewbox=\"0 0 320 124\">\n<rect fill=\"url(#vzGrid)\" height=\"124\" opacity=\"0.5\" width=\"320\"></rect>\n<g>\n<rect fill=\"none\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"rgba(242,240,236,0.14)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" width=\"112\" x=\"52\" y=\"22\"></rect>\n<rect fill=\"none\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"rgba(242,240,236,0.26)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" width=\"112\" x=\"72\" y=\"30\"></rect>\n<rect fill=\"rgba(123,140,255,0.10)\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"#7b8cff\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" width=\"112\" x=\"92\" y=\"38\"></rect>\n<path d=\"M108 88 L128 66 L142 80 L160 56 L188 90\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a3b0ff\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path>\n<circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"52\" fill=\"#a3b0ff\" r=\"5\"></circle>\n<rect fill=\"rgba(242,240,236,0.14)\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" width=\"56\" x=\"212\" y=\"46\"></rect>\n<rect fill=\"rgba(242,240,236,0.14)\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" width=\"40\" x=\"212\" y=\"60\"></rect>\n<rect fill=\"rgba(242,240,236,0.14)\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" width=\"48\" x=\"212\" y=\"74\"></rect>\n</g>\n</svg></span>\n<div class=\"article-card__top\"><span class=\"article-card__cat\">Creative strategy</span><span class=\"article-card__meta num\">Jul 28, 2026</span></div>\n<h3 class=\"article-card__title\">Why good creatives stop working</h3>\n<p class=\"article-card__excerpt\">Creative fatigue is usually diagnosed too late and treated with the wrong medicine. Here is what actually decays, how to see it three days earlier, and what to replace.</p>\n<div class=\"article-card_